---

## 📊 Current State Analysis

ObjectUI already has a solid view management foundation:

### ✅ What's Already Built

| Component | Location | Capability |
|-----------|----------|-----------|
| **ViewSwitcher** (plugin-view) | `packages/plugin-view/src/ViewSwitcher.tsx` | Tabs / Buttons / Dropdown switching between view types |
| **ViewSwitcher** (plugin-list) | `packages/plugin-list/src/ViewSwitcher.tsx` | Grid/Kanban/Gallery/Calendar/Timeline/Gantt/Map |
| **ObjectView** (plugin-view) | `packages/plugin-view/src/ObjectView.tsx` | Unified CRUD view with multi-view, named views, navigation |
| **ObjectView** (console) | `apps/console/src/components/ObjectView.tsx` | Airtable-style named-view tabs, URL routing |
| **ViewDesigner** | `packages/plugin-designer/src/ViewDesigner.tsx` | Create/edit view configs (columns, filters, sort, type) |
| **useViewSharing** | `packages/react/src/hooks/useViewSharing.ts` | Save/delete/duplicate/share views with visibility |
| **View Switching Tests** | `packages/react/src/__tests__/view-switching.test.tsx` | State preservation (selection, filters, scroll, sort) |

### Current UX Flow (from Screenshot)

Your demo shows an **Airtable-inspired** tab bar: `All Tasks | Board | Calendar | Active` with a "进入设计模式" (Enter Design Mode) button. The toolbar has `Hide fields | Filter | Group | Sort | Color | Comfortable` controls.

---

## 🔍 Gap Analysis: ObjectUI vs. Mainstream Platforms

### Comparison Matrix

| Capability | Salesforce | Power Apps | Airtable | Zoho | **ObjectUI** | Gap |
|-----------|-----------|-----------|---------|------|-------------|-----|
| Named views (pre-configured) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | — |
| View type switching (Grid↔Board↔Calendar) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | — |
| Inline view creation (one-click) | ✅ | ⚠️ | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ | **Gap A** |
| View rename inline | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | **Gap B** |
| View duplication | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ (hook only) | **Gap C** |
| View delete with confirmation | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ (designer only) | **Gap D** |
| Drag-reorder view tabs | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | **Gap E** |
| View context menu (right-click) | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | **Gap F** |
| Personal vs. shared views | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ (hook exists) | **Gap G** |
| Pin/favorite views | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | **Gap H** |
| View filter indicator (badge) | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | **Gap I** |
| "Save as new view" from current filters | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ (no UI) | **Gap J** |
| View overflow (many views → "More" dropdown) | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | **Gap K** |

---

## 🎯 Recommended Improvements (Prioritized)

### Phase 1: Quick Wins — View Tab Management UX (1-2 weeks)

These close the biggest UX gaps with the least effort:

#### 1A. Inline "Add View" Button on Tab Bar

Currently the "Add View" is buried in a dropdown menu. Salesforce and Airtable show a `+` button directly on the tab bar.

```typescript name=ViewTabBar-proposed-schema.ts
// Proposed enhancement to ObjectViewSchema
interface ObjectViewSchema {
  // ... existing props

  /**
   * View tab bar configuration
   * Controls inline view management UX
   */
  viewTabBar?: {
    /** Show inline "+" button to create new views */
    showAddButton?: boolean;       // default: true
    /** Allow inline renaming by double-clicking tab */
    inlineRename?: boolean;        // default: true
    /** Show context menu on right-click */
    contextMenu?: boolean;         // default: true
    /** Allow drag-reorder of view tabs */
    reorderable?: boolean;         // default: false
    /** Max visible tabs before overflow → "More" dropdown */
    maxVisibleTabs?: number;       // default: 6
    /** Show filter/sort indicator badges on tabs */
    showIndicators?: boolean;      // default: true
  };
}
```

#### 1B. View Tab Context Menu (Right-click)

Salesforce's right-click on a list view tab → `Rename | Duplicate | Delete | Share | Set as Default`

```tsx name=ViewTabContextMenu-concept.tsx
// Concept: Right-click context menu on view tabs
// Would live in apps/console/src/components/ObjectView.tsx

import { ContextMenu, ContextMenuContent, ContextMenuItem, ContextMenuSeparator, ContextMenuTrigger } from '@object-ui/components';

function ViewTab({ view, isActive, onRename, onDuplicate, onDelete, onSetDefault, onShare }: ViewTabProps) {
  return (
    <ContextMenuTrigger asChild>
      <button
        onClick={() => onViewChange(view.id)}
        onDoubleClick={() => onRename(view.id)}
        className={cn(
          "inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium border-b-2 transition-colors",
          isActive ? "border-primary text-primary" : "border-transparent text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
        )}
      >
        <ViewIcon className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
        {view.label}
        {view.hasActiveFilters && (
          <span className="ml-1 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary" />
        )}
      </button>
    </ContextMenuTrigger>
    <ContextMenuContent>
      <ContextMenuItem onClick={() => onRename(view.id)}>
        <Pencil className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" /> Rename
      </ContextMenuItem>
      <ContextMenuItem onClick={() => onDuplicate(view.id)}>
        <Copy className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" /> Duplicate View
      </ContextMenuItem>
      <ContextMenuItem onClick={() => onShare(view.id)}>
        <Share2 className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" /> Share View
      </ContextMenuItem>
      <ContextMenuItem onClick={() => onSetDefault(view.id)}>
        <Star className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" /> Set as Default
      </ContextMenuItem>
      <ContextMenuSeparator />
      <ContextMenuItem onClick={() => onDelete(view.id)} className="text-destructive">
        <Trash2 className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" /> Delete View
      </ContextMenuItem>
    </ContextMenuContent>
  );
}
```

#### 1C. View Overflow ("More" Dropdown)

When there are 7+ views, the tab bar overflows. Airtable solves this with a "..." overflow button.

```tsx name=ViewTabOverflow-concept.tsx
// Concept: Overflow handling for many view tabs
function ViewTabBar({ views, activeViewId, maxVisible = 6 }: ViewTabBarProps) {
  const visibleViews = views.slice(0, maxVisible);
  const overflowViews = views.slice(maxVisible);

  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-0.5 border-b px-3 overflow-hidden">
      {visibleViews.map(view => (
        <ViewTab key={view.id} view={view} isActive={view.id === activeViewId} />
      ))}

      {overflowViews.length > 0 && (
        <DropdownMenu>
          <DropdownMenuTrigger asChild>
            <button className="px-2 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
              <MoreHorizontal className="h-4 w-4" />
              <span className="ml-1 text-xs">{overflowViews.length} more</span>
            </button>
          </DropdownMenuTrigger>
          <DropdownMenuContent align="end">
            {overflowViews.map(view => (
              <DropdownMenuItem key={view.id} onClick={() => onViewChange(view.id)}>
                <ViewIcon type={view.type} className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
                {view.label}
              </DropdownMenuItem>
            ))}
          </DropdownMenuContent>
        </DropdownMenu>
      )}

      {/* Inline add button — always visible */}
      <button onClick={onAddView} className="px-2 py-2 text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <Plus className="h-4 w-4" />
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Phase 2: "Save Current State as View" (1 week)

The biggest missing pattern from Salesforce — the ability to apply filters/sort/group, then click "Save as New View" without entering the full ViewDesigner.

```tsx name=SaveAsViewDialog-concept.tsx
// Quick "Save as View" dialog
// Triggered from toolbar when user has active filters/sort that differ from the view definition

interface SaveAsViewDialogProps {
  objectName: string;
  currentFilters: Record<string, any>;
  currentSort: Array<{ field: string; direction: 'asc' | 'desc' }>;
  currentViewType: ViewType;
  currentColumns: string[];
  onSave: (config: { name: string; visibility: 'private' | 'shared' }) => void;
}

function SaveAsViewButton({ hasUnsavedChanges, onSave, onReset }: {
  hasUnsavedChanges: boolean;
  onSave: () => void;
  onReset: () => void;
}) {
  if (!hasUnsavedChanges) return null;

  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-1 ml-2 text-xs text-amber-600">
      <AlertCircle className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      <span>Unsaved changes</span>
      <Button variant="ghost" size="sm" onClick={onSave}>Save</Button>
      <Button variant="ghost" size="sm" onClick={onReset}>Reset</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Phase 3: View Type Quick-Switch Palette (1 week)

Instead of requiring a new named view for each type, allow quick-switching the *current view's type* like Notion's "Layout" menu:

```tsx name=ViewTypeQuickSwitch-concept.tsx
// A command palette for switching view type within the current view
// Similar to Notion's "Layout" dropdown

const VIEW_TYPE_OPTIONS = [
  { type: 'grid',     label: 'Table',    icon: Table,           description: 'Rows and columns' },
  { type: 'kanban',   label: 'Board',    icon: LayoutGrid,      description: 'Group by status' },
  { type: 'calendar', label: 'Calendar', icon: Calendar,        description: 'Events on a calendar' },
  { type: 'gallery',  label: 'Gallery',  icon: Images,          description: 'Visual cards' },
  { type: 'timeline', label: 'Timeline', icon: Activity,        description: 'Chronological order' },
  { type: 'gantt',    label: 'Gantt',    icon: GanttChartSquare,description: 'Project scheduling' },
  { type: 'map',      label: 'Map',      icon: MapPin,          description: 'Geographic view' },
] as const;

// This would be a popover/command triggered from a "Layout" button in the toolbar
```

### Phase 4: Drag-to-Reorder View Tabs (Optional, 1-2 days)

Low priority but differentiating — Airtable allows dragging tabs to reorder. Can be added using `@dnd-kit/sortable` (already likely in dependencies for Kanban).

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Recommendation

Based on the code scan, I recommend these specific changes:

### A. Enhance `ViewSwitcherSchema` in `@object-ui/types`

```typescript name=enhanced-view-types.ts
// Enhancement to packages/types/src/views.ts

export interface ViewTabBarConfig {
  /** Show inline "+" button to create views */
  showAddButton?: boolean;
  /** Allow inline tab rename via double-click */
  inlineRename?: boolean;
  /** Right-click context menu */
  contextMenu?: boolean;
  /** Drag-reorder tabs */
  reorderable?: boolean;
  /** Max visible tabs before overflow */
  maxVisibleTabs?: number;
  /** Show filter/sort badges on tabs */
  showIndicators?: boolean;
  /** Show "Save as View" when filters differ from saved */
  showSaveAsView?: boolean;
}

// Add to ObjectViewSchema:
export interface ObjectViewSchema extends BaseSchema {
  // ... existing

  /** View tab bar UX configuration */
  viewTabBar?: ViewTabBarConfig;

  /** Callback when a view is created inline */
  onViewCreate?: string;

  /** Callback when a view is deleted */
  onViewDelete?: string;

  /** Callback when views are reordered */
  onViewReorder?: string;
}
```

### B. Refactor Console's ObjectView Tab Bar into a Reusable Component

Currently the tab rendering is inline in `apps/console/src/components/ObjectView.tsx`. Extract it into `@object-ui/plugin-view` as a `<ViewTabBar>` component so it's reusable:

```typescript name=component-extraction-plan.ts
// Move from: apps/console/src/components/ObjectView.tsx (inline JSX)
// Move to:   packages/plugin-view/src/ViewTabBar.tsx (reusable component)

// This allows:
// 1. Console to use it
// 2. Any SDUI consumer to use it via schema
// 3. Storybook isolation for testing
```

### C. Connect `useViewSharing` Hook to the Tab Bar UI

The hook at `packages/react/src/hooks/useViewSharing.ts` already supports `saveView`, `deleteView`, `duplicateView`, `setVisibility` — but **there's no UI wired to it**. The context menu and "Save as View" patterns complete this connection.

---

## 📋 Implementation Priority Summary

| # | Enhancement | Effort | Impact | Inspired By |
|---|-----------|--------|--------|------------|
| 1 | Inline `+` Add View button on tab bar | 2h | 🔴 High | Airtable, Salesforce |
| 2 | Right-click Context Menu on view tabs | 1d | 🔴 High | Salesforce, Notion |
| 3 | Tab overflow → "More" dropdown | 4h | 🟡 Medium | Airtable |
| 4 | Filter/Sort badge indicator on tabs | 2h | 🟡 Medium | Salesforce, Airtable |
| 5 | "Save as New View" from current state | 2d | 🔴 High | Salesforce, Zoho |
| 6 | Inline tab rename (double-click) | 4h | 🟡 Medium | Airtable |
| 7 | View type quick-switch palette | 1d | 🟡 Medium | Notion |
| 8 | Extract `ViewTabBar` as reusable component | 1d | 🟡 Medium | Architecture |
| 9 | Drag-reorder view tabs | 1d | 🟢 Low | Airtable |
| 10 | Pin/favorite views | 4h | 🟢 Low | Salesforce |

**Total estimated effort: ~2 weeks for all 10 items.**

Items 1-5 (the top 5) deliver 80% of the UX improvement and can be done in **~1 week**.
